            </div>
            <CodeBlock size="sm" code={clientSnippets.cli} lang="bash" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-gray-400">A successful CLI round trip prints <code>hello krabka</code>. To inspect a producer example's record, run the CLI consumer without <code>--max-messages 1</code>, then press Ctrl+C to stop.</p>
      <section aria-labelledby="javascript-project" class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-white/10 p-5 space-y-4">
        <h3 id="javascript-project" class="font-semibold text-white">Run the JavaScript example as a project</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-300">Install Node.js with npm. After the local quickstart, download this project in a separate terminal and run it. It uses the same pinned KafkaJS dependency and producer code as the Node.js tab. A delivery failure exits with an error.</p>
        <button type="button" class="copy-btn rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 text-sm text-gray-300 hover:bg-white/10" data-copy={javascriptRunCode} aria-label="Copy JavaScript example setup">Copy setup</button>
        <CodeBlock code={javascriptRunCode} lang="bash" />
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">The record value is <code>Hello Krabka from KafkaJS!</code>. Use the CLI consumer with <code>--from-beginning</code> and without <code>--max-messages 1</code> to read the topic, then press Ctrl+C to stop. <a href={getPath('/quickstart/javascript/app.cjs')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">Download source</a> · <a href={getPath('/quickstart/javascript/package.json')} class="text-krab-400 underline underline-offset-2">Download package manifest</a></p>
